          "caption": "Fujairah Fort in UAE\nFujairah Fort (Arabic: قلعة الفجيرة‎) is a fort in the city of Fujairah, United Arab Emirates (UAE). Dating back to the 16th century, it is the among the oldest as well as the largest castles in the country. It is noted for playing significant roles in fighting back the wave of colonialism. Today, it is among the main tourist attractions in the city.[1] It is probably the oldest fort in the UAE and was occupied by the Wahhabists.",
